            <ArticleTitle>PTCA procedure for Shepherd's Crook right coronary artery lesion with a new long soft-tip 6F guiding catheter.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>390-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A new Cordis Long Brite Tip 6F guiding catheter (I.D. .064&quot;) is described. Because of its technical characteristics, this product provides greater balloon catheter support by means of deeper intubation of the right coronary artery (RCA). We present our experience with a Shepherd's Crook RCA lesion PTCA procedure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
